completed_at: "2026-08-08T22:59:48.214Z"
claim_principal: pi-agent
author: pi-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Every spawnSync site audited and assigned a tier with justification; silent-degradation sites (itemStatus, loadAppliedByTransaction) throw a named error on a status===null overrun instead of returning empty/absent; regression test drives itemStatus past Node's 1 MiB default and asserts the real status returns; mutation-tested (reverting each fix fails its test); full gate green (typecheck, coverage thresholds unchanged, audit, pack); standalone-loadability preserved."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-08T22:59:39.151Z",pi-agent,"Acceptance evidence:\n\nGates (all green):\n- npm run typecheck: clean.\n- npm run coverage: index.ts 83.01% lines / 77.51% branches / 88.54% funcs; thresholds 81/74/88 UNCHANGED, no c8 ignore (coverage rose vs baseline 82.68/76.75/88.42).\n- npm run build: clean.\n- npm run audit:prod: 0 vulnerabilities.\n- npm run pack:dry-run: 9 files, packs.\n- Full suite: 114 tests pass (109 prior + 5 new in test/buffer-regression.test.ts).\n\nPer-call-site tier assignment (see PR body for the full table):\n- itemStatus (pm get): tier-2. Was the only read on Node's 1 MiB default AND mapped null status onto undefined (silent \"item missing\"). Now maxBuffer + assertPmOutputFit.\n- loadAppliedByTransaction (pm list-all): tier-2. Had maxBuffer (#41) but swallowed null/error into an empty applied map (silent re-import). Now assertPmOutputFit.\n- loadKeyIndex, buildCsvExport (pm list-all): tier-2. Already threw on error (#41); unchanged (loud, not silent).\n- upsertCreate create/close, upsertUpdate update/close: tier-2. Added maxBuffer + assertPmOutputFit.\n- compensateCreate update/close: tier-2. Added maxBuffer only (best-effort rollback tolerates failure by design; no assert).\n- Tier-1 (in-process SDK read) NOT used: a static @unbrained/pm-cli value import breaks documented standalone-loadability (confirmed ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND loading dist/ off the package resolution path); task forbids dynamic import(); ctx.sdk.client.list carries a read-output budget. Verified standalone load is PRESERVED after the fix.\n\nMutation test results (revert fix in scratch, confirm new test FAILS, restore):\n- Revert itemStatus (drop maxBuffer+assert): \"itemStatus returns the real status ... exceeds 1 MiB\" FAILS, \"itemStatus surfaces a buffer overrun as a named error\" FAILS. Restored -> pass.\n- Revert loadAppliedByTransaction assert: \"loadAppliedByTransaction surfaces a buffer overrun as a named error\" FAILS. Restored -> pass.\nBoth new tests are load-bearing (fail without the fix).\n\nRegression coverage of the fix:\n- A read path (itemStatus) driven past Node's 1 MiB default (2 MiB body via --body-file) returns the REAL status, not undefined.\n- A tier-2 site (itemStatus AND loadAppliedByTransaction) under a capped PM_LIST_MAX_BUFFER surfaces the overrun as a named error, not an empty/absent result."
close_reason: "Fixed: every pm spawnSync site audited and tier-assigned. The two silent-degradation sites (itemStatus, loadAppliedByTransaction) now route a status===null stdout overrun through assertPmOutputFit as a hard, named error instead of returning empty/absent; itemStatus also gained the maxBuffer it lacked. Writes carry maxBuffer too. Tier-1 in-process SDK read not used (static import breaks documented standalone-loadability; dynamic import forbidden; ctx.sdk.client.list is budgeted) — verified standalone load preserved. Full gate green, thresholds unchanged, mutation-tested, 5 regression tests added."
body: ""
